DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection in civetweb standalone server.
  The cmd parameter is routed through an exec_args_t struct (I3). A strict
  metachar sanitizer (S3) is present but only activates with --strict-exec;
  omitting it leaves the endpoint fully exploitable.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 -- config file):
  mechanism:  Key=value config file parsed by read_exec_config() into
              exec_cfg {enabled, logging}. prescan_exec_args() strips
              --config PATH from argv before civetweb's parser.
  check:      exec_handler() returns 404 unless exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging
  complexity: requires modelling fopen->fgets->sscanf data flow into struct fields

INPUT_FLOW (I3 -- struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  ->  ri->query_string
  path:       exec_handler() sets args.cmd = qs+4, args.flags = 0;
              system(args.cmd)
  transforms: pointer through exec_args_t struct

SANITIZATION (S3 -- config-gated metachar check):
  mechanism:  static int strict_exec in exec_handler; if strict_exec:
              strpbrk(qs+4, "|;&`$") -> reject 403
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec; strict_exec stays 0, check never runs

SINK:        system(args.cmd) in exec_handler() (src/main.c)

